{
  "sections": {
    "main": {
      "type": "bengkung-guide",
      "blocks": {
        "quote_1": {
          "type": "quote",
          "settings": {
            "quote": "My youngest is 17, and my stomach still looks exactly as it did when I left the delivery room. Do I have to accept it?",
            "cite": ""
          }
        },
        "text_2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>No. But you must stop doing what makes the problem worse. Tight shapewear, years of crunches and diets often address the front while the body wraps all the way around.</p>"
          }
        },
        "heading_3": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Ordinary shapewear compresses the front. Your body goes all the way around."
          }
        },
        "image_4": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0794/0797/2593/files/ADV_2.png?v=1779041950&width=900",
            "caption": "Postpartum profile",
            "hide_caption": true,
            "narrow": false,
            "fallback_image": ""
          }
        },
        "quote_5": {
          "type": "quote",
          "settings": {
            "quote": "I lost every pregnancy pound, but the shape of my stomach was permanently different. Exercise changed nothing.",
            "cite": ""
          }
        },
        "quote_6": {
          "type": "quote",
          "settings": {
            "quote": "At 49, I no longer recognized myself in the mirror.",
            "cite": ""
          }
        },
        "heading_7": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What nobody told you"
          }
        },
        "image_8": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0794/0797/2593/files/ADV_3_1.jpg?v=1779041974&width=900",
            "caption": "Postpartum exercise",
            "hide_caption": true,
            "narrow": false,
            "fallback_image": ""
          }
        },
        "text_9": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Walking, swimming, yoga and rigid shapewear may leave the same structural problem untouched. Classic crunches and sit-ups can increase outward pressure instead of bringing the abdominal wall inward.</p>"
          }
        },
        "button_10": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Discover BLK_MAJESTY →",
            "link": "shopify://products/culotte-post-patrum",
            "note": ""
          }
        },
        "heading_11": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The signs I recognized because I lived them"
          }
        },
        "text_12": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A stomach that protrudes before breakfast. A ridge that appears when standing up. Clothes that fall differently even when your weight is unchanged. A silhouette that looks more rounded in the evening than in the morning.</p>"
          }
        },
        "heading_13": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The appointment that changed everything"
          }
        },
        "image_14": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0794/0797/2593/files/1f37cf93-9e4d-46e0-a7b5-64c5c7b19c71.png?v=1778794749&width=900",
            "caption": "Medical consultation",
            "hide_caption": true,
            "narrow": false,
            "fallback_image": ""
          }
        },
        "text_15": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A colleague placed two fingers above my navel and explained abdominal separation. The relief was immediate: it was not a personal failure, and weight alone was not the issue.</p>"
          }
        },
        "pull_16": {
          "type": "pull",
          "settings": {
            "text": "It wasn’t my fault.\nNobody had explained it."
          }
        },
        "heading_17": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The structure behind the silhouette"
          }
        },
        "image_18": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0794/0797/2593/files/3aa7e50f-f2a4-4147-917b-0e76a8162320.png?v=1778794954&width=900",
            "caption": "Abdominal anatomy",
            "hide_caption": true,
            "narrow": false,
            "fallback_image": ""
          }
        },
        "text_19": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>During pregnancy, the abdominal muscles move apart to make room. For many women the gap persists for years. A gentle, circular support can visually hold the abdomen from the front, sides and back.</p>"
          }
        },
        "callout_20": {
          "type": "callout",
          "settings": {
            "title": "A simple at-home check",
            "text": "<p>Lie on your back with your knees bent. Place two fingers above your navel and gently lift your head. A visible ridge or a gap can be a reason to speak with a qualified healthcare professional.</p>"
          }
        },
        "heading_21": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Inspired by the Bengkung wrap"
          }
        },
        "image_22": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0794/0797/2593/files/Design_sans_titre_20.png?v=1778795518&width=900",
            "caption": "Woman wearing high-waist briefs",
            "hide_caption": true,
            "narrow": false,
            "fallback_image": ""
          }
        },
        "text_23": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The cross-band design distributes support around three zones. It is built as an everyday high-waist brief: easy to put on, smooth under clothes and comfortable through ordinary movement.</p>"
          }
        },
        "heading_24": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Day 8—something changed"
          }
        },
        "image_25": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0794/0797/2593/files/ADV_7.jpg?v=1778795554&width=900",
            "caption": "Woman fastening jeans",
            "hide_caption": true,
            "narrow": false,
            "fallback_image": ""
          }
        },
        "text_26": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The jeans I had not closed since my second pregnancy finally buttoned without holding my breath. My waist looked present again.</p>"
          }
        },
        "heading_27": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Six weeks later"
          }
        },
        "image_28": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0794/0797/2593/files/ADV_8.jpg?v=1778795589&width=900",
